From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mt76: dma: ensure headroom before inserting alignment pad

mt76_insert_hdr_pad() pushes two bytes without checking headroom.  Forwarded
frames can arrive with no spare headroom and trigger skb_under_panic.  Make
the skb writable with the required headroom before inserting the pad.

The WARN_ONCE is a local diagnostic, not part of the fix: mt76x02 asks
mac80211 for exactly two bytes of extra_tx_headroom, so by contract this
should never be short.  It fires only in the exact case that used to panic
(a pad is actually needed and there is no room for it) and prints the caller,
so the path handing over the tight skb can be identified before anything is
reported upstream.  Drop it once the caller is known.

Signed-off-by: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
--- a/dma.c
+++ b/dma.c
@@ -671,8 +671,23 @@
 	txwi = mt76_get_txwi_ptr(dev, t);
 
 	skb->prev = skb->next = NULL;
-	if (dev->drv->drv_flags & MT_DRV_TX_ALIGNED4_SKBS)
+	if (dev->drv->drv_flags & MT_DRV_TX_ALIGNED4_SKBS) {
+		/* Diagnostic only: catch whoever hands us an skb that cannot
+		 * take the two-byte pad. Same condition mt76_insert_hdr_pad()
+		 * would have pushed on, so it stays quiet for frames that do
+		 * not need the pad at all.
+		 */
+		if (unlikely(skb_headroom(skb) < 2 &&
+			     ieee80211_get_hdrlen_from_skb(skb) % 4))
+			WARN_ONCE(1,
+				  "mt76: hdr pad without headroom: dev=%s headroom=%u len=%u cloned=%d shared=%d\n",
+				  skb->dev ? skb->dev->name : "none",
+				  skb_headroom(skb), skb->len,
+				  skb_cloned(skb), skb_shared(skb));
+		if (skb_cow_head(skb, 2))
+			goto free;
 		mt76_insert_hdr_pad(skb);
+	}
 
 	len = skb_headlen(skb);
 	addr = dma_map_single(dev->dma_dev, skb->data, len, DMA_TO_DEVICE);
